00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.116 line:82% align:center
What finally broke
it was that we

00:00:03.116 --> 00:00:06.231 line:82% align:center
ran out of money
and had to cut the

00:00:06.231 --> 00:00:06.800 line:82% align:center
price.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.114 line:82% align:center
We went from a
seat-based plan to a flat

00:00:10.114 --> 00:00:13.192 line:82% align:center
monthly one because
it was simpler to

00:00:13.192 --> 00:00:14.800 line:82% align:center
explain in a panic.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.548 line:82% align:center
Revenue went up
forty percent in six

00:00:17.548 --> 00:00:18.350 line:82% align:center
weeks.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.750 line:82% align:center
Not because the
price was better.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.593 line:82% align:center
Because the product
finally matched the

00:00:23.593 --> 00:00:25.550 line:82% align:center
shape of the
person using it.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.462 line:82% align:center
If I were starting
again, the thing I

00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:31.268 line:82% align:center
would do differently
is I would ship the

00:00:31.268 --> 00:00:34.203 line:82% align:center
smallest possible
version to the smallest

00:00:34.203 --> 00:00:37.353 line:82% align:center
possible audience
and I would refuse to

00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:40.496 line:82% align:center
write down who the
customer is for six

00:00:40.496 --> 00:00:41.100 line:82% align:center
months.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.100 line:82% align:center
Let the usage tell you.
